[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]What REDcode is[/color][/b][/size]

REDcode is built by [url=https://edgemodders.ai/]EDGEmodders[/url], a modding community whose idea is simple: [b]anyone can mod[/b]. It brings the game's files into VS Code, the editor most modders and AI assistants already use.

REDcode stands on [b]WolvenKit[/b]. Every game file is read and written by WolvenKit's own libraries, which run in [b]REDbridge[/b], a small local program that REDcode downloads, starts and talks to. Projects are WolvenKit's own [i].cpmodproj[/i] projects, byte for byte, so they move freely between REDcode and WolvenKit. Credit for the file formats, the archive reader, the importers and exporters, and years of research belongs to the WolvenKit team and contributors.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Highlights[/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]The game's archives as a tree[/color][/b][/size]
Every file in the game, in folders, with search as you type (by file name, path, or a clothing item's in-game name such as [i]comfy rocker[/i]) and a filter that narrows the tree while you type ([i]osprey mesh[/i], [i]ep1\weapons\*.xbm[/i]). Open any file read-only, or add it to your project for an editable copy.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]A real CR2W editor[/color][/b][/size]
.ent, .app, .mesh, materials, scenes and the rest open as a tree and a property grid: dropdowns for enums, add and remove in arrays, undo and redo, search across the whole file. Localization files open as a table you edit in place. Atlases open on their texture with every part drawn over it, to move and resize.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Edgemodders/REDcode/main/nexus/images/cr2w-editor.webp[/img]

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]New files from nothing[/color][/b][/size]
Right-click a folder in your project and choose [b]New File...[/b]: a texture from your own image (as color, normal map, mask or UI), an ink atlas on its texture, a material instance on the base material you pick, an empty entity, appearance or multilayer setup, or a copy of any game file under a new name. TweakXL, ArchiveXL and Redscript files start in the folders the game reads them from. Names are checked as game paths, and an image with odd sides can be resized for you.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Textures, meshes and sounds[/color][/b][/size]
Textures show as images. Meshes open in 3D: orbit, pick the LOD, switch appearances, turn submeshes on and off, see each one's material. [b]Find Items[/b] lists the game's items that wear the mesh, with their names in the game. [b]Open in EDGEmat[/b] takes the mesh to [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/EDGEmat]EDGEmat[/url] to change its materials. Voice lines and sound effects play in a player with a waveform, and [b]Browse Game Sounds[/b] lists the game's 73,000 sound effects as events to filter and play. [b]Replace[/b] swaps a sound effect for a WAV of yours in one step, all of an event's variations at once if you like, ready for Pack and Play. The 3D views light like the game, with reflections, a brightness control and a fixed light to see how shine moves.

[color=#19f3ff][i][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Edgemodders/REDcode/main/nexus/images/textures-meshes-sounds.webp[/img][/i][/color]

[color=#19f3ff][size=4][b]Full Blender Round-Trip Editing[/b][/size][/color]

[color=#ffffff][size=3]View in REDcode, launch the model into Blender, make edits and save, the save imports seamlessly back into REDcode.[/size][/color]
[color=#19f3ff][i][img width=406]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Edgemodders/REDcode/main/nexus/images/blender-1.webp[/img][img width=418]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Edgemodders/REDcode/main/nexus/images/blender-2.webp[/img][/i][/color]


[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]The TweakDB, browsable[/color][/b][/size]
Every record type and record, with a page per record where links take you to the records it names, LocKeys show their text and resource paths open the file. [b]New Tweak from This Record[/b] writes a TweakXL file that clones or changes it, every flat listed and ready to uncomment. Hover a record path in a tweak file to see what it is.

[color=#19f3ff][i][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Edgemodders/REDcode/main/nexus/images/tweakdb-record-1.webp[/img][/i][/color]
[color=#19f3ff][i][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Edgemodders/REDcode/main/nexus/images/tweakdb-record-2.webp[/img][/i][/color]

[color=#00ffff][size=4][b]The game's texts, in 19 languages[/b] [/size][/color]
[b]The LocKeys view finds the text behind any [i]LocKey#[/i], and the LocKey behind any text, in the base game and Phantom Liberty. Click a result to open it in its file. One click adds it to your project's own text file, made and wired up for ArchiveXL if you have none, so you can change what the game says. Hover a LocKey in a tweak, a script or a CR2W file to read it. [/b]
[b][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Edgemodders/REDcode/main/nexus/images/lockeys.webp[/img][/b]

[color=#00ffff][size=4][b]Game animations[/b][/size][/color]
An [i].anims[/i] file opens on its animations: pick one and watch it play on a body (the base male or female body, or a character's own meshes when another tool asks) or as bones and joints, with play forward and backward, stop, single frames, jump to either end, a scrub bar, loop, speed, and a Root motion switch that moves the whole rig through the scene. A synced clip lists its set, the other clips of the same moment such as the Trauma Team's AV and soldiers landing, and [b]Play the Set[/b] plays them together, each placed where the game puts it.

[color=#00ffff][size=4][b]Animations from words[/b][/size][/color]
In the [b]Clip[/b] tab of a man's or woman's animation, say what it should show, and press [b]Generate[/b]: [url=https://uthana.com]Uthana[/url] makes the motion straight onto the game's own skeleton (with your own Uthana key, $0.10 a second, charged only when it finishes). It becomes a new clip in your project, or takes the place of a game clip, facing the way the game's clips face and with feet that respect the ground. [b]From a GLB[/b] does the same with a clip from Blender. Open a made clip again and its words are there, ready for another go.

[color=#00ffff][size=4][b]Edit made animations[/b][/size][/color]
The [b]Edit[/b] tab of a made clip fixes what words cannot: it shows where each foot slides and pins it, turns a bone or moves a hand or foot at a moment with an easing, lays another clip's motion on a hand or the upper body, trims and loops. Every step is kept and can be changed or taken out later, with Undo and Redo, and the clip as made is never lost. [b]Edit in Blender[/b] opens the clip on the body in Blender: each save there comes straight back as the clip's new start.

[color=#00ffff][size=4][b]Lip sync[/b][/size][/color]
[b]Open Lip Sync[/b] lists a character's lip synced lines, scene by scene. Pick one to hear it spoken on that character's own head, with every curve the game's clip moves under the voice: jaw, lips, tongue, brows, blinks. Type a new line and [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/EDGEwave]EDGEwave[/url] speaks it in the character's voice (your own ElevenLabs key), with the lip sync made to match. A voice line in the audio player and a lip sync set in the animation view open it at that line.

[color=#00ffff][size=4][b]The world in 3D[/b][/size][/color]
A [i].streamingsector[/i] opens in 3D: every building, prop and street mesh where the sector places it, with markers for lights, sounds and spawn points. Fly around with the right mouse button and W, A, S, D, or the camera buttons; double-click a thing to fly to it. Click a thing to see its node and its own materials, [b]Show in Tree[/b] to edit it, and [b]Coarser levels[/b] to add what the game draws from far away. Select many at once with Ctrl+click, a box on the screen or a [b]Volume[/b] in the world, then [b]Isolate[/b] them, add their meshes to your project or copy the list. [b]Overlaps[/b] lists the sectors that reach into this one, to see as see-through layers or in full and to pick in. [b]Properties[/b] shows what every selected thing shares and changes it on all of them at once. The search box selects what it finds ([i]soda[/i] selects the soda cans), and [b]Scripts[/b] runs small JavaScript files that find, select or change nodes, such as every streaming distance under 45 m, shown first and undone in one step.

[color=#00ffff][size=4][b]Pack, install, play[/b][/size][/color]
[b]Pack[/b] builds your mod the way WolvenKit does (Ctrl+Shift+B), [b]Install[/b] puts it in the game (through EDGEdeck when you have it, so you can undo it, and only your mod: other mods' changes wait for you), and [b]Run Game[/b] starts Cyberpunk. [b]Pack and Play[/b] does it in one click, straight into the running game: through [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/REDnode]REDnode[/url] and its REDswap when the game runs with it and its MCP server is on (edited sound banks too), or else it installs the mod for the next start. Export to glTF, PNG and WAV, edit, and import back: a GLB can become a new mesh, and edited sound effects go back into the game's sound banks. REDmod packs carry your custom sounds.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Works with the other EDGE tools[/color][/b][/size]
[b]Add to Library[/b] puts a game or project file in the EDGE Library, the store the EDGE tools share, with the files it needs, and the [b]Library[/b] view shows the Library and adds its items to your project, with [b]Refresh Project from Library[/b] when an item has a newer version. And a tool can claim the TweakDB records it is made for, so a click on one opens that tool.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]One place for your AI keys[/color][/b][/size]
The [b]Keys[/b] view keeps the AI service keys every EDGE tool shares, in VS Code and in the game (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, ElevenLabs, Tripo, Uthana and others): set one once, see which tools read it, and say which tools may.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]TweakXL files[/color][/b][/size]
Syntax highlighting, brackets, comments and snippets for TweakXL's [i].tweak[/i] format.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]For AI assistants[/color][/b][/size]
[url=https://www.npmjs.com/package/@edgemodders/redcode-mcp]@edgemodders/redcode-mcp[/url] gives Claude Code and other assistants the same engine: browse the archives, read and patch CR2W files, export, import, pack, query the TweakDB and the game's texts, make and edit animations, read lip sync, and read, change and script a sector's nodes. Ask your assistant to make the mod, and watch it work in the same project. With REDnode in the game, REDcode also tells REDnode mods and the assistants connected to it which project is open, so EDGEbuilder can place your own objects.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Coming next[/color][/b][/size]
Planned: [b]editing lip sync[/b] and putting new voiced lines into a mod, on any head; a [b]timeline[/b] for made animations, posed by grabbing a bone; [b]takes[/b] for made animations; changing a sector's materials live from EDGEmat; and the [b]REDnode loop[/b], to edit a REDnode mod and see it in the running game without a restart, with the game's logs and a debugger in VS Code.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit.[/*]
[*][url=https://code.visualstudio.com/]VS Code[/url] 1.70 or later, [url=https://vscodium.com/]VSCodium[/url], or EDGEkit.[/*]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 on PC: the Steam, GOG or Epic install. REDcode finds it.[/*]
[*]REDbridge: REDcode offers to download it on first start. Nothing to set up.[/*]
[*]The .NET 10 runtime, which REDbridge runs on. REDcode offers to install it when it is missing.[/*]
[*]Optional: [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/EDGEdeck]EDGEdeck[/url], for installs you can undo.[/*]
[/list]
[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Install[/color][/b][/size]

[b]From a store (recommended, updates itself):[/b] in VS Code, open the Extensions view (Ctrl+Shift+X), search for [b]REDcode for Cyberpunk 2077[/b] and click Install. Or open its [url=https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=Edgemodders.redcode-cyberpunk]Marketplace[/url] or [url=https://open-vsx.org/extension/edgemodders/redcode-cyberpunk]Open VSX[/url] page.

[b]From the file here:[/b]
[list]
[*]Download the main file with [b]Manual download[/b] and extract it anywhere.[/*]
[*]In VS Code, open the Extensions view (Ctrl+Shift+X), click [b]...[/b] at its top, choose [b]Install from VSIX...[/b] and pick [i]redcode-cyberpunk-<version>.vsix[/i].[/*]
[*]Click the REDcode icon in the activity bar. REDcode looks for the game and offers to download REDbridge.[/*]
[/list]
Do not install it with Vortex: it is not a game mod, and Vortex would put it in the game folder.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]The EDGE platform[/color][/b][/size]

REDcode is one of the EDGE tools. Each works on its own and together:

[list]
[*][b][url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/EDGEdeck]EDGEdeck[/url][/b]: a simple mod manager in VS Code. REDcode's Install goes through it.[/*]
[*][b][url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/REDnode]REDnode[/url][/b]: mods in JavaScript, web pages over the game, and REDagent, an AI assistant in the game. EDGEdeck knows REDnode packages and puts them in the right place. [/*]
[*][b][url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/REDbridge]REDbridge[/url][/b]: runs WolvenKit's libraries for REDcode, EDGEdeck and REDnode.[/*]
[*][b]The REDnode HUD theme[/b]: the dark, yellow and cyan theme REDcode's pages are drawn for, in the same stores.[/*]
[*][b][url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/EDGEkit]EDGEkit[/url][/b]: one editor with every EDGE tool built in.[/*]
[/list]
[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Questions[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Does it replace WolvenKit?[/b]
No. It runs WolvenKit's libraries and writes WolvenKit's projects, so you can switch between the two on the same project. Use whichever suits the task.

[b]Why is REDbridge a separate download?[/b]
WolvenKit's libraries are GPL-3.0 and run in .NET, so they live in their own program, REDbridge (GPL-3.0), which REDcode talks to. REDcode itself stays MIT. REDcode downloads REDbridge from its GitHub releases and tells you when there is a newer one.

[b]Will it change my game folder?[/b]
Only when you press Install (or Pack and Install), and only with your mod's files. Through EDGEdeck, an install can be undone exactly.

[b]Is it free?[/b]
Yes, and open source under the MIT license. The code is on [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/REDcode]GitHub[/url].

